# ============================================================================
# FILE HEADER - DOCKER IGNORE CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================================
# WHY: Define which files and directories should be excluded from Docker images
# HOW: Specifies patterns for files that should not be copied into the container
# WHAT: This file prevents including unnecessary files in the Docker build context
# MEANING: "Docker ignore rules - keeps images lightweight and secure"
# NOTE: This ensures Docker images stay small and don't include sensitive data,
#       caches, or development-only files that shouldn't be in production.
# ============================================================================

# ============================================================================
# SECTION 1 - VERSION CONTROL DIRECTORIES
# ============================================================================
# WHY: Git metadata is not needed inside the container
# HOW: Excludes .git directory and .github workflows
# WHAT: Prevents copying version control history into the image
# MEANING: "Don't include Git repository data in the Docker image"
.git
.github

# ============================================================================
# SECTION 2 - PYTHON VIRTUAL ENVIRONMENTS
# ============================================================================
# WHY: Virtual environments are host-specific and should not be copied
# HOW: Excludes both .venv and venv directories
# WHAT: Prevents copying Python virtual environment files
# MEANING: "Don't include local Python environments - Docker creates its own"
# NOTE: Docker installs dependencies fresh from requirements.txt, so local
#       virtual environments would only add unnecessary size to the image.
.venv
venv

# ============================================================================
# SECTION 3 - PYTHON CACHE AND COMPILED FILES
# ============================================================================
# WHY: Cache files are host-specific and regenerated automatically
# HOW: Excludes __pycache__, *.pyc, and various tool caches
# WHAT: Prevents copying Python bytecode and tool cache directories
# MEANING: "Don't include compiled Python files or tool caches"
# NOTE: These files are regenerated when Python runs, so including them
#       would only increase image size without any benefit.
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache

# ============================================================================
# SECTION 4 - ENVIRONMENT AND SECRET FILES
# ============================================================================
# WHY: Environment files contain secrets and host-specific configuration
# HOW: Excludes .env file which contains database credentials and API keys
# WHAT: Prevents committing secrets to the Docker image
# MEANING: "Don't include environment variables with secrets"
# NOTE: Secrets should be injected at runtime via Docker environment variables
#       or Docker secrets, never baked into the image itself.
.env

# ============================================================================
# SECTION 5 - GENERATED DATA FILES
# ============================================================================
# WHY: Data files are generated at runtime and should not be in the image
# HOW: Excludes CSV files in data/ directory
# WHAT: Prevents copying generated datasets into the image
# MEANING: "Don't include generated data - it's created when the pipeline runs"
# NOTE: Data is generated by the pipeline or mounted as volumes at runtime.
#       Including it in the image would make the image unnecessarily large.
data/*.csv

# ============================================================================
# SECTION 6 - GENERATED OUTPUT FILES
# ============================================================================
# WHY: Output files are generated during pipeline execution
# HOW: Excludes Markdown files in output/ directory
# WHAT: Prevents copying generated reports and documentation
# MEANING: "Don't include generated output - it's created at runtime"
output/*.md

# ============================================================================
# SECTION 7 - MACHINE LEARNING MODEL FILES
# ============================================================================
# WHY: Model files are large binary files that should be mounted or downloaded
# HOW: Excludes .joblib files in models/ directory
# WHAT: Prevents copying trained ML models into the image
# MEANING: "Don't include ML models - they're loaded from mounted volumes"
# NOTE: ML models are typically several MB in size. They should be mounted
#       as volumes or downloaded from a model registry, not baked into the image.
models/*.joblib

# ============================================================================
# SECTION 8 - DOCUMENTATION SCREENSHOTS
# ============================================================================
# WHY: Screenshots are for documentation only, not needed in the container
# HOW: Excludes screenshots directory in docs/
# WHAT: Prevents copying documentation images into the image
# MEANING: "Don't include documentation screenshots in the Docker image"
docs/screenshots

# ============================================================================
# SECTION 9 - PYTHON PACKAGE METADATA
# ============================================================================
# WHY: Package metadata is generated during installation
# HOW: Excludes *.egg-info directories
# WHAT: Prevents copying Python package metadata files
# MEANING: "Don't include package metadata - it's generated by pip install"
# NOTE: These files are created when installing the package and are not
#       needed in the Docker image since dependencies are installed fresh.
*.egg-info
